            "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    X = np.load(\"vectors.npy\")\n    N = X.shape[0]\n\n    # Precompute squared L2 norm of each row\n    norms_sq = np.sum(X * X, axis=1, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    total_dist = 0.0\n    block_size = 2000\n\n    for i in range(0, N, block_size):\n        i_end = min(i + block_size, N)\n        X_i = X[i:i_end]\n        norms_i = norms_sq[i:i_end, None]\n\n        for j in range(i, N, block_size):\n            j_end = min(j + block_size, N)\n            X_j = X[j:j_end]\n            norms_j = norms_sq[None, j:j_end]\n\n            # Compute pairwise squared distances: ||u - v||^2 = ||u||^2 + ||v||^2 - 2<u, v>\n            gram = X_i @ X_j.T\n            dist_sq = norms_i + norms_j - 2.0 * gram\n            np.maximum(dist_sq, 0.0, out=dist_sq)\n            dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq, out=dist_sq)\n\n            if i == j:\n                total_dist += np.sum(np.triu(dist, k=1), dtype=np.float64)\n            else:\n                total_dist += np.sum(dist, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    # Double to account for both (i, j) and (j, i) pairs; diagonal is 0\n    total_dist *= 2.0\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total_dist}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
